.TH UNHEADED\-AUTH 1 "2026-10-29" "unheaded 86590d34" "Unheaded Kingdom"
.SH NAME
unheaded\-auth \- Serve the Kingdom's login, JWKS and OIDC discovery endpoints; `unheaded\-auth user` manages the users file.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unheaded\-auth
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Serve the Kingdom's login, JWKS and OIDC discovery endpoints; `unheaded\-auth user` manages the users file.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B user add|list|del
manage users (see unheaded\-auth user \-\-help)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-audiences \fISTRING\fR
comma\-separated audiences a login may ask for; the first is the default (default unheaded)
.TP
.B \-\-dev\-plaintext
serve login, JWKS and discovery over plain HTTP (development only)
.TP
.B \-\-issuer\-url \fISTRING\fR
external issuer URL: the tokens' iss and the discovery base (required)
.TP
.B \-\-key\-file \fISTRING\fR
issuer Ed25519 key (unheaded\-keygen unheaded\-auth), 0400 (default /etc/unheaded/keys/unheaded\-auth.key)
.TP
.B \-\-listen \fISTRING\fR
listen address (default :19020)
.TP
.B \-\-users\-file \fISTRING\fR
users file (unheaded\-auth user add), 0600 (default /etc/unheaded/auth/users.json)
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
display this help and exit
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
output version information and exit
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unheaded (1)
